{"r":"gzw","lane":{"p":2257,"e":[{"h":"غَزَاهُ","t":["[aor. ,] inf. n. ",[2,"غَزْوٌ"],", ",[1,"He willed,"]," or ",[1,"desired, it; he sought it;"]," and ",[1,"he aimed at it, intended it,"]," or ",[1,"meant it;"]," syn. ",[2,"أَرَادَهُ"],"; and ",[2,"طَلَبَهُ"],"; and ",[2,"قَصَدَهُ"],"; [the first of which is often used in the same senses as the second and third;] as also ↓ ",[2,"اغتزاهُ"],"; (K, TA;) this last mentioned by ISd as syn. with ",[2,"قَصَدَهُ"],". (TA.) One says, ",[2,"عَرَفْتُ مَا"],[2,"يُغْزَى مِنْ هٰذَا الكَلَامِ"]," i. e. [",[1,"I knew,"]," or, emphatically, ",[1,"I know,"],"] ",[1,"what is willed"]," or ",[1,"desired"]," (",[2,"مَا يُرَادُ"],") [",[1,"from this speech"],"]. (S.) And ",[2,"غَزْوِى"],[2,"كَذَا"],[1,"My aim,"]," or ",[1,"intention,"]," or ",[1,"meaning, is such a thing."]," (K.) ― -b2- [Hence, app.,] ",[2,"غَزَا العَدُوَّ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"غَزْوٌ"]," (S, Mgh, Msb, K) and ",[2,"غَزَوَانٌ"],", (K, TA,) or, as some say, ",[2,"غَزْوَانٌ"],", mentioned by Sb, (TA,) and ",[2,"غَزَاوَةٌ"],", (K,) [but see what is said of this last at the close of this paragraph,] ",[1,"He went forth,"]," (Er-Rághib, TA,) or ",[1,"repaired,"]," or ",[1,"betook himself,"]," (Mgh,) ",[1,"to wage war,"]," (Er-Rághib, TA,) or ",[1,"to fight,"]," (Mgh,) ",[1,"with the enemy;"]," (Er-Rághib, Mgh, TA;) or ",[1,"he went to fight with, and plunder, the enemy;"]," (K, TA;) ",[1,"in the country of the latter."]," (Msb.) [And ",[2,"غَزَا"]," alone, the objective complement being understood, often signifies the same; or ",[1,"He engaged in a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition,"]," or ",[1,"in such expeditions."],"] ― -b3- And ",[2,"غَزَا إِلَيْهِ"],", inf. n. as above, ",[1,"He tended, repaired, betook himself,"]," or ",[1,"went, to,"]," or ",[1,"towards, him,"]," or ",[1,"it;"]," syn. ",[2,"قَصَدَهُ"],". (TA.) -A2- ",[2,"غَزَاوَةٌ"],", mentioned above, is of a measure which in most instances is that of an inf. n. of an intrans. verb, and it seems to be an inf. n. of which the verb is ",[2,"غَزُوَ"],", meaning ",[2,"جَادَ غَزْوُهُ"]," [i. e. ",[1,"Excellent,"]," or ",[1,"how excellent, is his engaging in a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition,"]," or ",[1,"in such expeditions!"],"]; and to be similar to ",[2,"قَضُوَ"]," meaning ",[2,"جَادَ قَضَآءُهُ"],", and ",[2,"ضَرُبَتْ يَدُهُ"]," meaning ",[2,"جَادَ ضَرْبُهَا"],". (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"غَزَّوَ","t":["see what next follows."],"f":"2"},{"h":"اغزاهُ","t":[[1,"He fitted him out, equipped him,"]," or ",[1,"furnished him,"]," (S,) or ",[1,"he sent him,"]," (Mgh, Msb,) or ",[1,"he urged,"]," or ",[1,"incited, him,"]," (K,) ",[1,"to engage in a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition,"]," (S, * Mgh, * Msb, * K,) ",[1,"in the country of the enemy;"]," (Msb;) and ↓ ",[2,"غزّاهُ"]," signifies the same. (K.) -A2- ",[2,"أَغْزَتْ"],", said of a woman, (Mgh, K,) ",[1,"Her husband was absent"]," [",[1,"engaged in a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition, in the country of the enemy"],"]; (Mgh;) or ",[1,"her husband went"]," [or ",[1,"had gone"],"] ",[1,"to fight with, and plunder, the enemy."]," (K.) ― -b2- And, said of a she-camel, ",[1,"Her impregnation was,"]," or ",[1,"became, difficult."]," (S, K.) -A3- And ",[2,"اغزاهُ"],[1,"He granted him some delay, and deferred"]," [",[1,"the exacting of"],"] ",[1,"the debt that he owed."]," (S, K.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"اغتِزاهُ","t":[": see 1, first sentence. -A2- ",[2,"اغتزى بِفُلَانٍ"],[1,"He had such a one peculiarly to himself from among his companions:"]," (K, TA:) like ",[2,"اِغْتَزَّ بِهِ"],". (TA.) A poet says, ",[2,"قَدْ يَغْتَزِى الهِجْرَانُ بِالتَّجَرُّمِ"]," [",[1,"Sometimes,"]," or ",[1,"often, the cutting off from friendly intercourse has the accusation of that which is a crime,"]," or ",[1,"a fault,"]," or ",[1,"an offence, peculiarly assigned to it"]," (",[1,"as the cause"],")]: ",[2,"التجرّم"]," here meaning ",[2,"اِدِّعَآءُ"],[2,"الجُرْمِ"],". (TA.)"],"f":"8"},{"h":"غَزَاةٌ","t":[": see the next paragraph, in three places."]},{"h":"غَزْوَةٌ","t":["The ",[1,"act of"]," [",[2,"الغَزْو"]," i. e.] ",[1,"repairing to fight with"]," [or ",[1,"to fight with and plunder"],"] ",[1,"the enemy"]," [",[1,"in the country of the latter"],"]; as also ↓ ",[2,"غَزَاةٌ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"مَغْزَاةٌ"],": (Mgh:) or the first signifies ",[1,"a single time"]," [or ",[1,"act"],"] ",[1,"of"],[2,"الغَزْو"]," [i. e. ",[1,"a single warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition"],"]; (Th, Msb, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"مَغْزَاةٌ"],": (Msb:) and ↓ ",[2,"غَزَاةٌ"]," is the subst. from ",[2,"غَزَوْتُ العَدُوَّ"]," [as such meaning as expl. above, i. e. the ",[1,"act of"],[2,"الغَزْو"],"]: (S, TA:) or this signifies [",[1,"a campaign,"]," i. e.] the ",[1,"work"]," [or ",[1,"operations"],"] ",[1,"of a year:"]," (Th, TA:) the pl. (of ",[2,"غَزْوَةٌ"],", Msb, [and of ↓ ",[2,"غَزَاةٌ"],", for this is originally ",[2,"غَزَوَةٌ"],",]) is ",[2,"غَزَوَاتٌ"],", and (of ↓ ",[2,"مَغْزَاةٌ"],", Msb) ",[2,"مَغَازٍ"],", (Mgh, Msb,) which latter pl. is applied to the ",[2,"غَزَوَات"]," of Mohammad. (TA.)"]},{"h":"غِزْوَةٌ","t":[[1,"i. q."],[2,"طِلْبَةٌ"]," [app. as meaning ",[1,"A mode,"]," or ",[1,"manner, of seeking, &c."],"]. (TA.)"]},{"h":"أَبُو غَزْوَانَ","t":["[or ",[2,"غَزْوَانٍ"],"?] ",[1,"The cat:"]," because it is ever making war upon the mouse. (",[2,"يَغْزُو الفَأْرَ أَبَدًا"],"). (Har p. 663.)"]},{"h":"غَزْوِىٌّ","t":["accord. to [many, app., of] the copies of the S; or ",[2,"غَزَوِىٌّ"],", accord. to ISd, [and so in some copies of the S,] said by ISd to be altered from the regular form [which is ",[2,"غَزْوِىٌّ"],"]; (TA;) ",[1,"Of,"]," or ",[1,"relating to,"],[2,"الغَزْو"]," [or ",[1,"the making a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition"],"]. (S, ISd, TA.)"]},{"h":"غَزِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"غَازٍ"],"."]},{"h":"غَزَّآءٌ","t":["One ",[1,"who engages much,"]," or ",[1,"often, in warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expeditions;"]," syn. ",[2,"كَثِيرُ"],[2,"الغَزْوِ"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"غَازٍ","t":["One ",[1,"going,"]," or ",[1,"who goes, to fight with, and plunder, the enemy,"]," (S, * Mgh, * Msb, K,) ",[1,"in the country of the latter;"]," (Msb;) [one ",[1,"engaging,"]," or ",[1,"who engages, in a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition:"]," and ",[1,"a warrior,"]," in a general sense:] pl. ",[2,"غُزَاةٌ"]," (S, Mgh, Msb) and ",[2,"غُزًّى"]," (S, Msb, K, TA, in the CK ",[2,"غُزّىٰ"],") and ",[2,"غُزَّآءٌ"]," (S) and ",[2,"غُزِىٌّ"],", (K,) [originally ",[2,"غُزُوىٌ"],",] of the measure ",[2,"فُعُولٌ"],", (TA,) and ↓ ",[2,"غَزِىٌّ"]," is pl. of [the pl.] ",[2,"غُزَاةٌ"],", (S, Msb,) or [rather] a quasi-pl. n.; (K;) and ↓ ",[2,"غَازِيَةٌ"]," signifies ",[1,"a company,"]," or ",[1,"body, of"],[2,"غُزَاة"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"غَازِيةٌ","t":[": see what immediately precedes."]},{"h":"الاغزآء","t":["and ",[2,"المغزى"]," [app. ",[2,"الأَغْزَآءُ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"المَغْزَى"],", the former a pl. of which the sing. is not mentioned, and the latter a quasi-pl. n. like ",[2,"المَرْجَلُ"]," from ",[2,"الرَّجُلُ"],",] ",[1,"The offspring"]," (",[2,"نَتَائِج"]," [more properly ",[2,"نِتَاج"],", which agrees with the context,]) ",[1,"of the"]," [",[1,"season called"],"] ",[2,"صَيْف"],", on the authority of IAar, [meaning ",[1,"such offspring of camels,"]," for it is added,] ",[1,"which are discommended, the young camel thereof being always weak."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَغْزًى","t":["The ",[1,"intended sense"]," of a saying; the ",[1,"meaning"]," thereof; syn. ",[2,"مَقْصَدٌ"]," [as an inf. n. used in the sense of the pass. part. n. of its verb]. (S, K; in the CK written ",[2,"مَقْصِد"],".) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"مَغْزَاةٌ"],". -A2- And see the paragraph next preceding this."]},{"h":"مُغْزٍ","t":["[act. part. n. of 4, q. v.]. ― -b2- ",[2,"مُغْزِيَةٌ"]," A woman ",[1,"whose husband is absent;"]," (Mgh;) [meaning] one ",[1,"whose husband has gone to fight with, and plunder, the enemy."]," (S, * TA.) See an ex. in a trad. mentioned voce ",[2,"كَاسِرٌ"],". -A2- Also, ",[2,"مُغْزِيَةٌ"],", A she-camel ",[1,"that has exceeded the year"]," [",[1,"from the time when she was covered"],"] ",[1,"without bringing forth;"]," like ",[2,"مِدْرَاجٌ"],": (El-Umawee, S:) or a she-camel ",[1,"that has exceeded the year by a month,"]," (K, TA,) or ",[1,"the like thereof,"]," (TA,) ",[1,"in pregnancy:"]," (K, TA:) so in the M. (TA.) And A she-ass ",[1,"that is late in bringing forth, but does then bring forth."]," (S.) ",[2,"المُغْزِى مِنَ الغَنَمِ"]," means ",[1,"Those that are late in bringing forth, by a month,"]," or ",[1,"two months, after the others, of the sheep"]," or ",[1,"goats, because of their having conceived at a late period."]," (TA.) ― -b2- And ",[2,"مغْزٍ"]," signifies A she-camel ",[1,"whose impregnation is difficult:"]," mentioned by Az. (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَغْزَاةٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"غَزْوَةٌ"],", in three places. ― -b2- Also ",[1,"A place of"],[2,"غَزْو"]," [meaning ",[1,"making a warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expedition"],"]: pl. ",[2,"مَغَازٍ"],". (TA.) ― -b3- And ",[2,"المَغَازِى"]," signifies also ",[1,"The memorable deeds of the"],[2,"غُزَاة"]," [meaning ",[1,"those who engage in warring,"]," or ",[1,"warring and plundering, expeditions,"]," pl. of ",[2,"غَازٍ"],"]: (K, TA:) in which sense, some say, it has no sing., but others say that its sing. is ",[2,"مَغْزَاةٌ"]," or ↓ ",[2,"مَغْزًى"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَغْزِىٌّ","t":["[as pass. part. n. of ",[2,"غَزَا"],"] was used as an epithet applied to a man: it is properly with ",[2,"و"]," [i. e. ",[2,"مَغْزُوٌّ"],"]; but there are many instances of the former kind. (TA.)"]}]},"maqayis":["الغين والزاء والحرف المعتل أصلان صحيحان، أحدهما طلب شيء، والآخر في باب اللقاح.","فالأول الغزو. ويقال: غزوت أغزو. والغازي: الطالب لذلك، والجمع غزاة وغزي أيضا، كما يقال لجماعة الحاج حجيج. والمغزية: المرأة التي غزا زوجها. ويقال في النسبة إلى الغزو: غزوي.","والثاني: قولهم: أغزت الناقة، إذا عسر لقاحها. وقال قوم: الأتان المغزية: التي يتأخر نتاجها ثم تنتج. قال الهذلي: يرن على مغزيات العقا ... ق يقرو بها قفرات الصلال"],"mufradat":["الغزو: الخروج إلى محاربة العدو، وقد غزا يغزو غزوا، فهو غاز، وجمعه غزاة وغزى. قال تعالى: أو كانوا غزى [آل عمران/ 156] ."]}